    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Here is the text from Section 4.2:\n\n\"4.2 Price Adjustments: The base rate for fuel shall be reviewed quarterly. While any permanent changes to the fuel contract require mutual written consent from both SwiftRoute and the Supplier, the Supplier reserves the right to implement a temporary surcharge of up to 5% on all deliveries during peak seasonal months (defined in Exhibit B) without prior notice to SwiftRoute, to account for market volatility.\"\n\nSo, based on that, are we safe from them just raising prices on us whenever they want? Does this section give them any unilateral rights to change the rates unexpectedly?",
      "source": "evaluator"
